<% content_for :title, "Installation — Shadwire" %>
<% content_for :description, "Requirements, installing the shadwire CLI, what init does to your Rails app, and how to add your first component." %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <%= tag.style rouge_stylesheet %>
<% end %>

<article class="space-y-12">
  <%= render "docs/header",
        title: "Installation",
        description: "Install the CLI, run init once, and start adding components." %>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Requirements") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      The installed components only need what a Rails app usually has. These are the minimum
      versions:
    </p>

    <%= render "docs/table",
          headers: [ "Requirement", "Version", "Why" ],
          rows: [
            [ docs_code("ruby"), ">= 3.2", "The syntax the components and the CLI use." ],
            [ docs_code("rails"), ">= 7.1", "View helpers, the tag builder and the asset pipeline." ],
            [ docs_code("view_component"), ">= 4.0", "The components are ViewComponent classes." ],
            [ docs_code("lucide-rails"), ">= 0.7", "The Rails port of Lucide, shadcn/ui's icon set." ],
            [ "Tailwind CSS", "v4", safe_join([ "The tokens use ", docs_code("@theme inline"), ", which is v4." ]) ]
          ] %>

    <%= render layout: "docs/callout", locals: { icon: "triangle-alert", title: "Interactive components need Stimulus" } do %>
      <%= registry_stimulus_component_count %> of the <%= docs_component_items.size %> components ship a Stimulus controller. They
      install into <code>app/javascript/controllers/</code> and register themselves through
      <code>importmap-rails</code>' default <code>eagerLoadControllersFrom</code>. If your app
      registers controllers by hand, register the new ones too.
      <code>bin/shadwire status --json</code> shows what it detected under <code>stack</code>.
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Install the CLI") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      The CLI is only used during development, never at runtime. You can install it globally
      or add it to the app.
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:install_cli], language: :shell) %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Run init") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Run it from the root of the Rails app. It is the only command you run without
      <code>bin/</code>, because it is the one that creates the binstub the other commands use.
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:init], language: :shell) %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">What it does:</p>

    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <% [
        [ "shadwire.json", "writes the manifest at the app root: the registry URL, where each kind of file goes, the Tailwind entrypoint, and what is installed." ],
        [ "Base files", "installs app/components/ui_component.rb (the shared superclass) and vendor/shadwire/shadwire.css (the tokens)." ],
        [ "Base gems", "adds view_component and lucide-rails to the Gemfile if they are missing." ],
        [ "development group", "adds shadwire itself to the Gemfile's development group." ],
        [ "bin/shadwire", "writes the binstub you run the CLI with from then on. It loads the CLI from the app's bundle." ],
        [ "Tailwind @import", "imports shadwire.css in the Tailwind entrypoint." ]
      ].each do |label, body| %>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <%= ui_icon("check", size: :sm, class: "mt-1 shrink-0 text-primary") %>
          <span><strong class="font-semibold text-foreground"><%= label %></strong>: <%= body %></span>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Running it again is safe: it does not undo anything, and it leaves an existing binstub
      alone. <%= docs_code("--force") %> resets <%= docs_code("shadwire.json") %> and rewrites
      the binstub.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Why bin/shadwire") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      After init, run every command through <%= docs_code("bin/shadwire") %>. The binstub loads
      the CLI from the app's bundle, so everyone on the project runs the same version, whatever
      they have installed globally.
    </p>

    <%= render layout: "docs/callout", locals: { icon: "triangle-alert", title: "A bundle without the development group has no CLI" } do %>
      <code>bundle install --without development</code>, common in deploys and some CI jobs,
      does not install <code>shadwire</code>, so <code>bin/shadwire</code> will not run there.
      Any job that uses the CLI, such as a drift check, needs the development group.
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Add your first component") %>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:add], language: :shell) %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      The components it depends on are installed along with it. Each component also installs
      its own helper module (<%= docs_code("button") %> writes
      <%= docs_code("app/helpers/ui/button_helper.rb") %>), and Rails includes everything under
      <%= docs_code("app/helpers/") %> in your views with no <%= docs_code("include") %>.
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:usage]) %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Both forms render the same thing. In views, the helper is shorter.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Confirm it worked") %>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:status], language: :shell) %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      <%= docs_code("status") %> never fails. Outside a Rails app it reports
      <%= docs_code('"rails": false') %>, an unreachable registry shows up as
      <%= docs_code("registryError") %> and an unreadable <%= docs_code("shadwire.json") %> as
      <%= docs_code("configError") %>, and the exit code is always 0. The
      <%= link_to "CLI", docs_cli_path, class: "font-medium underline underline-offset-4" %> page
      lists every field.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Without the CLI") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      You can copy the files by hand from the
      <%= link_to "published registry", docs_registry_path, class: "font-medium underline underline-offset-4" %>
      or from <%= link_to "llms-full.txt", docs_llms_txt_path, class: "font-medium underline underline-offset-4" %>,
      but then <%= docs_code("shadwire.json") %> does not know about them, and
      <%= docs_code("diff") %>, <%= docs_code("update") %> and <%= docs_code("remove") %>
      rely on it. Use the CLI when you can.
    </p>
  </section>
</article>
